{"term":"sacanear","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"sexual_misbehavior","concept":"sexual_misbehavior","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":40,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":98,"recognition_pct_peak":98,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"To engage in sexual naughtiness or mischief with someone; derived from 'sacana' (scoundrel, dirty-minded person); implies sexual shenanigans or messing around rather than intercourse specifically.","english_term":"to fool around","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The primary non-sexual meaning is 'to trick, cheat, or mess with someone'; the sexual sense is a secondary connotation via the adjective 'sacana' (lewd/roguish); the noun 'sacanagem' covers both trickery and sexual naughtiness, making this term semantically broader than any single English equivalent."}
