{"term":"boquete","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"blowjob","concept":"fellatio","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":75,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The most common Brazilian Portuguese slang for a blowjob; oral stimulation of the penis performed on a partner.","english_term":"blowjob","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Derived from 'boca' (mouth); the default slang term throughout Brazil across all age groups and regions; considered crude but not extreme; also spelled 'boquête' in some orthographic conventions; the near-total recognition rate reflects how thoroughly it has displaced clinical alternatives in everyday speech."}
{"term":"boquetão","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"blowjob","concept":"fellatio","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Augmentative of 'boquete'; denotes an enthusiastic, thorough, or extended blowjob; implies notably greater depth, duration, or skill than a standard 'boquete.'","english_term":"a really good blowjob","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The augmentative suffix '-ão' intensifies along multiple dimensions simultaneously (size, thoroughness, quality); some speakers use it specifically to imply deep-throat technique; others use it hyperbolically for any particularly satisfying or prolonged blowjob; no single English term captures the augmentative nuance precisely."}
{"term":"chupar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"oral_sex_generic","concept":"oral_sex_generic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to suck'; the most common verb for performing oral sex on any partner; applies to both fellatio and cunnilingus depending on context.","english_term":"to suck off","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Primary meaning is simply 'to suck' (candy, through a straw, etc.); sexual meaning is context-dependent and universally understood; one of the most versatile oral-sex verbs in Brazilian Portuguese precisely because it does not specify the genital involved."}
{"term":"mamar","lang":"pt-BR","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"blowjob","concept":"fellatio","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":70,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to breastfeed or suckle'; used as crude slang for performing oral sex, most commonly fellatio.","english_term":"to go down on","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Primary meaning is infant nursing; the sexual connotation derives from the intimate oral-suckling motion; more commonly implies fellatio than cunnilingus though technically applicable to both; the transfer from nursing to sex gives the word a distinctive taboo charge absent in 'chupar'; the word also appears in the phrase 'mamar gostoso' (to suck deliciously) as explicit praise."}
